From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: camcc-sdm845: round shared PLL parent rates

The 808 MHz camera PLL actually runs at 808000195 Hz. When an RCG that
propagates rate changes to its parent asks for the nominal 808 MHz, the
clock framework sees a new parent rate, although the PLL would stay at
the same achievable rate, and recalculates and reprograms the PLL's
other children. Their recalculated rates can then select the next
frequency table entry, and with it a parent that isn't running. This
happens through the ordinary CSI PHY timer RCGs as well as through the
shared RCGs, and breaks the camera clocks while other camera blocks are
running.

Have determine_rate return the rate the parent can actually achieve,
while the RCG keeps its canonical frequency, so that an unchanged PLL
isn't reprogrammed. The other RCG operations, and RCGs that don't
propagate rate changes to their parent, are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c | 70 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
index 534dc56fc1..0887c8d59f 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sdm845.c
@@ -17,6 +17,27 @@
 #include "clk-regmap.h"
 #include "gdsc.h"
 
+static struct clk_ops cam_cc_shared_ops;
+static struct clk_ops cam_cc_rcg_ops;
+
+static int cam_cc_determine_rate(struct clk_hw *hw, struct clk_rate_request *req)
+{
+	long parent_rate;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = clk_rcg2_ops.determine_rate(hw, req);
+	if (ret || !(clk_hw_get_flags(hw) & CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT))
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Avoid reprogramming siblings for the fractional PLL rounding error. */
+	parent_rate = clk_hw_round_rate(req->best_parent_hw, req->best_parent_rate);
+	if (parent_rate < 0)
+		return parent_rate;
+
+	req->best_parent_rate = parent_rate;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 enum {
 	P_BI_TCXO,
 	P_CAM_CC_PLL0_OUT_EVEN,
